# Terraform.
#
# The patterns below are intentionally unanchored (no leading path). A pattern
# like `terraform/*.tfstate` only matches a *top-level* terraform/ directory,
# so it missed cloud-infrastructure/terraform/environments/*/terraform.tfstate
# entirely. State files hold the RDS master password in plaintext, so a missed
# match here means committing a live credential.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
tfplan
*.auto.tfvars
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored — it pins provider versions
# and hashes, and belongs in version control so every machine and CI run
# resolves the same providers.

# EC2 key pairs created for one-off manual bootstrap tasks (e.g. a temporary
# SSH bastion) — a live private key, never committed.
*.pem

cdk.out/
build/
mywork.txt
# Local run logs from starting a service in the background
*.err

# LocalObjectStore driver root (ADR-007): raw dealer uploads and inter-stage
# payloads. Never committed — recreated on demand.
.storage/
DEPLOYMENT-GAPS.md

# ingestion-tester's per-run output (generated CSV/ZIP/HTML report) and the
# large one-off scratch CSVs manually generated during ETL testing — both
# regenerated on demand by vehicle-generator.ts / image-generator.ts /
# ingestion-tester.ts, never meant to be committed. Named explicitly rather
# than by a broad glob so this never shadows the committed fixtures
# (test-data/6_rows.csv, 100_rows.csv, 120_rows.csv, 6_rows_images.zip).
ingestion-service/test-runs/
ingestion-service/test-data/300_rows*.csv
ingestion-service/test-data/10_rows.csv
ingestion-service/test-data/3_dirty_rows.csv

# Local-only notes (deployment values etc.)
*.local.md
